      "side": 1,
      "message": "Given the change to `gfxstream_vk_private.h` and that entry points are created by a `genrule`/ not checked-in / not visible, please create a `guest/vulkan_enc/README.md` or `guest/vulkan/README.md` that explains the new flow across the layers.\n\nI guess ideally you could start with a snippet like:\n\n```\n// [1]\nauto* vkGetInstanceProcAddr \u003d dlsym(\u003cgfxstream lib\u003e, \u0027vkGetInstanceProcAddr\u0027);\n\n// [2]\nauto* vkCreateInstance \u003d vkGetInstanceProcAddr(VK_NULL_HANDLE, \u0027vkCreateInstance\u0027);\n\n// [3]\nVkInstance instance \u003d vkCreateInstance(...);\n\n// [4]\nauto* vkCreateDevice \u003d vkGetInstanceProcAddr(instance, \u0027vkCreateDevice\u0027);\n\n// [5]\nauto* vkGetDeviceProcAddr \u003d vkGetInstanceProcAddr(instance, \u0027vkGetDeviceProcAddr\u0027);\n\n// [6]\nVkDevice device \u003d vkCreateDevice(...);\n\n// [7]\nauto* vkAllocateMemory \u003d vkGetDeviceProcAddr(device, \u0027vkAllocateMemory\u0027);\n\n// [8]\nVkDeviceMemory memory \u003d vkAllocateMemory(...);\n```\n\nand show a snippet of a generated entry point with links to the mesa docs, explain that `VkInstance` from `// [3]` is really a `gfxstream_vk_instance` with a link to `guest/vulkan_enc/gfxstream_vk_private.h`, explain that `gfxstream_vk_instance::internal_object` is really a `goldfish_instance` with a link to `guest/vulkan_enc/Resources.h`, explain how the call from `vkAllocateMemory()` hits the mesa function and then the ResourceTracker function and then VkEncoder function, etc.",
